[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514066523","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99893#issuecomment-2514066523","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99893","id":2514066523,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V2Zxb","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T09:56:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T09:57:03Z","body":"> Seems fine, but I'm not sure if we should add a new public function for a few edge cases.\r\n> \r\n> Adding temporary `CharString` when both length and data are used if definitely a good change.\r\n\r\nI would say that in my opinion, it makes sense to give access to operations the current code already do (as there is no new code in this PR), which can enable more robust and concise code. However I do understand that you want to keep your public API as clean as possible for all users and that it may not make sense in this regard to add them. I don't think 2 functions would really hurt readability and I think these are operations you would want to have in such a class. But I'm biased so if people really think it's not usefull, I'll revert it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514066523/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523855013","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99893#issuecomment-2523855013","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99893","id":2523855013,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Wbvil","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T17:54:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T17:54:20Z","body":"I agree with bruvzg with respect to exposing new functions to users. In general we should only ever increase the API surface for core classes when there is a real user demand. We should never increase the API surface simply because we can. \r\n\r\nThat being said, I don't see anything in this PR that exposes new functions to users? Has that code already been removed?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523855013/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523995215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99893#issuecomment-2523995215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99893","id":2523995215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WcRxP","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T19:19:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T19:19:28Z","body":"> I agree with bruvzg with respect to exposing new functions to users. In general we should only ever increase the API surface for core classes when there is a real user demand. We should never increase the API surface simply because we can.\r\n> \r\n> That being said, I don't see anything in this PR that exposes new functions to users? Has that code already been removed?\r\n\r\nDeclaring those two functions : \r\n`uint32_t utf8_length() const;`\r\n`static uint32_t unicode_codepoint_as_utf8_length(char32_t c);`\r\nin ustring.h","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523995215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550779444","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99893#issuecomment-2550779444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99893","id":2550779444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YCc40","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T09:15:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T09:15:27Z","body":"@bruvzg @clayjohn So what do you think ? Do I close this PR ? Do I just remove the utf8_length function and just keep this as removing duplicate `utf8()` calls ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550779444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550801687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99893#issuecomment-2550801687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99893","id":2550801687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YCiUX","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T09:20:44Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T09:20:44Z","body":"> Do I just remove the utf8_length function and just keep this as removing duplicate utf8() calls ?\r\n\r\nProbably this. My only concern is that the existence of the public function will lead to misuse (it's easy to assume you are supposed to use both `utf8` and `utf8_length` every time you are converting string to UTF-8).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550801687/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0